      {
        "id": 218913,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-06-06T19:57:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yeah, \"Muerto\" suggests that the character is himself dead.&nbsp; One who makes use of the dead (a necromancer of some sort) would probably use \"muerte\" or some derivation thereof.&nbsp; Also, this shoots down the all-female theory (or it would be \"Muerta\").</p><p>\"Headlong\" sure does sound like a double entendre for someone with a literally long head.&nbsp; Maybe a psychic, maybe a stretcher (we don't really have one of them yet).&nbsp; It wouldn't be a bad name for Tempest's offspring, either, since Tempest is considered hotheaded by Maerynian standards, and their child would be even moreso.</p>",
        "post_number": 30,
        "post_type": 1,
